cifs: fix max_credits implementation

jira KERNEL-814
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10
commit-author Shyam Prasad N <sprasad@microsoft.com>
commit 5e90aa21eb1372736e08cee0c0bf47735c5c4b95
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10/5e90aa21.failed

The current implementation of max_credits on the client does
not work because the CreditRequest logic for several commands
does not take max_credits into account.

Still, we can end up asking the server for more credits, depending
on the number of credits in flight. For this, we need to
limit the credits while parsing the responses too.

	Signed-off-by: Shyam Prasad N <sprasad@microsoft.com>
	Signed-off-by: Steve French <stfrench@microsoft.com>
(cherry picked from commit 5e90aa21eb1372736e08cee0c0bf47735c5c4b95)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	fs/cifs/smb2pdu.c
